{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["And the word <b>וְחָטָאת</b> is a past tense verb, and the vav converts it to future, as is the rule, for it is like <b>וְחָטְאָה</b>. And since they suppressed the alef, as it is in the word <b>חָטָא</b>, and they cannot place a hidden [letter] after alef, therefore they substituted the heh with tav. And there is no need for any dagesh in the tav. And like it: <b>וְקָרָאת אֶתְכֶם הָרָעָה</b> (Deut. 31:29). And <b>הָעָם</b> in this place is feminine, like <b>הָעָם אֲשֶׁר בְּקִרְבָּהּ יוֹשֶׁבֶת לָבֶטַח</b> (Judg. 18:7), <b>מַדּוּעַ שָׁבוּבָה הָעָם הַזֶּה</b> (Jer. 5:5). And the meaning is that the sin will be upon you, and it is a way of rebuke, for the sin will be upon His name. And like it: <b>וְהָיִיתִי אֲנִי וּבְנִי שְׁלֹמֹה חַטָּאִים</b> (1 Kings 1:21), <b>וְאוֹיְבֵינוּ יָלִיעֲגוּ לָמוֹ</b> (Ps. 80:7), <b>וַיָּמִירוּ אֶת כְּבוֹדָם</b> (Ps. 106:20)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "I read כנו as כינו ('they thus framed it'); the text as given lacks the yod."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:04.812097561Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}